Firefox --proxy requires a fresh profile; omit --profile to preserve user preferences
Usage: compat_report [--browser chrome|firefox] [--headed|--headless]
[--output DIR] [--profile DIR] [--proxy http://HOST:PORT] [--viewport WIDTHxHEIGHT]
[--timeout-secs 1..300] [--idle-timeout-secs 1..300] [HTTP(S)_URL ...]
Defaults: headless Chrome, 1280x800, 30s per operation, 5s idle wait.
Browser shutdown allows at least 6s for its bounded graceful cleanup.
Without URLs observes Mercari, Rakuma, X, YouTube, TikTok and Instagram.
Exit0: requested operations completed (HTTP denial can still be observed).
Exit1: an operation/report failed; attribution to driver/site is undetermined.
Exit2: invalid arguments. Output directory must be new or empty.
--proxy accepts an explicit HTTP proxy without credentials; Firefox requires a fresh profile.
